    "body": "## Stage 7.15 - ATOM 7: Instant hover toast hints\n\n**User authorization (2026-10-14):<redacted>\n\n### Evidence from current main (baseline: `28b6a25ce9459b8ab223b72d7dc9977d785c46bd`)\n- `AsyncScene/Web/index.html` lines ~95-98: four topbar `.statIcon` elements use native `title` (\"Влияние\", \"Репутация\", \"Баланс\", \"Победы\").\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js` lines ~916-929: `syncTopbarStatTitles()` dynamically writes `title` for four kinds; lines ~1774-1805 also write/remove native `title` on point-cap and REP-cap surfaces (`.pointsWrap`, `#mePointsOverflow`, `#mePoints`, `#meRepNeed`).\n- `ui-core.js` ~982-1144: `showDeltaToastInstant`, `UI.showStatToast`, `UI.showActionToast` create internal `.statToast` immediately and already dismiss on clicking **that toast**.\n- `ui-profile-visual-tone-repair.js` ~1300-1380: `stage6UnifiedStatToast` with click dismissal; `COALESCE_MS=90` is a **stat message coalescing delay**, NOT a hover tooltip delay. Do not change coalescing in this task.\n- `ui-menu.js` lottery toast is an independent app-managed click-to-dismiss element; other `title` use in `ui-boot.js`, `ui-menu.js` may be unrelated controls, not automatically in scope.\n- Accepted canon `.ai-memory/CANON.md`: production toasts persist until clicking the exact toast and must dismiss independently; no TTL/automatic dismissal.\n\n### Codex action scope\n1. Read current repository policy/memory and verify current main, branch occupancy, published source/docs mirrors. Start with a **source+runtime inventory** of every hover affordance of *toast/stat notification UI*: native `title` and custom `toast/hint`. Record selectors, source writers, real trigger and delay cause; do not guess based only on text.\n2. For affected native tooltip surfaces, implement lightweight internal **immediate** tooltip on hover/focus (first event/render, no delayed timer or transition wait); remove native `title` there to prevent a late second browser tooltip. Preserve tooltip text/profile variations, cap messaging, touch/tap behavior, keyboard focus access, aria semantics and accessible labels.\n3. Keep transient hover hints distinct from **persistent notification toasts**: hints may close on pointerleave/blur; stat/event/action/lottery toasts must never auto-dismiss on hover leave, timers or animation and remain individually clickable until dismissal. Showing a hint must not consume or dismiss an existing toast, modify its content, prevent user clicks, or clear sibling stat-toast.\n4. Scope is tooltip presentation, not stat delta timing, profile logic, NPC/game rules, economy, persistence or 90-ms coalescing.\n5. Add actually executed regression checks (native title absent on migrated active DOM, instant pointerenter/focus hint, no timers, proper pointerleave/blur/touch behavior, independent two+ stat-toast click-to-dismiss, profile changes, repeat hovers) and run relevant existing Stage 6 stat-toast + Stage 7.15 regressions. Prefer permitted built-in Codex Browser for actual visual behavior; no Chromium/Playwright or page.evaluate if repository policy prohibits.\n6. Keep exact `AsyncScene/Web/**` and `docs/**` mirrors, cache-busting where required. One scoped new branch from *current* main, one Draft PR; CI, evidence, exact HEAD for ChatGPT review. Codex does NOT merge or claim user Safari acceptance. Work is excluded. Do not start unrelated Stage 7.15 milestones.\n\n### Acceptance\nAll in-scope native delayed hover descriptions replaced by visible instant custom hints on desktop Safari; no duplicate native popup; correct on focus and when profile changes; internal hints unchanged or faster only if source-verified delay; persistent toasts still click-to-dismiss individually with full independence.",
